&#8220;I am not even thinking about casting right now,&#8221; Chu told Variety &#8216;s Marc Malkin. &#8220;We&#8217;re just trying to get the story right.&#8221;

That story is currently sitting with writer Liz Meriwether, who is adapting Spears&#8217; bestselling 2023 memoir The Woman in Me for the big screen. Chu has already taken a peek at some of Meriwether&#8217;s work, and while he was careful not to reveal too many details, he had some enthusiastic words to share about what he&#8217;s seen.

&#8220;She&#8217;s doing so many beautiful things and I may or may not have gotten glimpses of what she&#8217;s been doing and it&#8217;s incredible,&#8221; he said. &#8220;It&#8217;s incredible, profound, beautiful. And that&#8217;s all I can say about it. You already got me to say too much.&#8221;

The director said he receives &#8220;hundreds of emails&#8221; from people around the world sending in unsolicited auditions for the beloved role, but he isn&#8217;t ready to start making casting decisions just yet. No actors have officially been announced for the project.

Chu also played coy when asked whether he&#8217;s been spending time with Spears herself, responding, &#8220;I cannot say anything right now.&#8221;

The film was first announced in 2024 after Universal Pictures acquired the rights to Spears&#8217; memoir, with Chu attached to direct and Marc Platt producing. Meriwether, best known for creating New Girl and co-creating Dying for Sex , joined the project as a screenwriter earlier this year.

Meriwether previously told Variety that adapting Spears&#8217; life into a feature film has required her to think differently about storytelling. &#8220;I haven&#8217;t written for a movie in a long time,&#8221; she said in August. &#8220;It&#8217;s just trying to think in a two-hour story as opposed to like an eight-hour story.&#8221;
